the CNRI portion of “Python-2.0” is coming from or where it is used.\r\n(3)\tThere’s an additional “ZERO-CLAUSE BSD LICENSE FOR CODE IN THE PYTHON DOCUMENTATION” license section at the end.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/867091133/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/867093505","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200#issuecomment-867093505","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200","id":867093505,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg2NzA5MzUwNQ==","user":{"login":"ariel11","id":17935946,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTM1OTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17935946?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11","html_url":"https://github.com/ariel11","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ariel11/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-23T19:15:39Z","updated_at":"2021-06-23T19:16:00Z","body":"To summarize the three examples above - the consistent differences between the SPDX \"Python-2.0\" and the licenses used in the wild are as follows:\r\n\r\n1. The dates in PYTHON SOFTWARE FOUNDATION LICENSE VERSION 2, Section 2 are different.\r\n2. The CNRI section is different - uses the text from the \"CNRI-Python-GPL-Compatible” SPDX without the click-accept language.\r\n3. The name \"Python\" is \"Python 3.9.5\" in Example 1.\r\n4. There is sometimes an additional ZERO-CLAUSE section, as specified above. \r\n\r\n\r\nCc: @capfei for visibility","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/867093505/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/867787139","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200#issuecomment-867787139","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200","id":867787139,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg2Nzc4NzEzOQ==","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-24T16:34:18Z","updated_at":"2021-06-24T16:34:18Z","body":"discussed research @ariel11 did on June 24 call: decision to add as stack similar to what we did for Python-2.0 as it appears on https://docs.python.org/3/license.html\r\n\r\nHowever, question around this language on that page:\r\n\"Starting with Python 3.8.6, examples, recipes, and other code in the documentation are dual licensed under the PSF License Agreement and the Zero-Clause BSD license.\"\r\n\r\nIn examples above (and seemingly consistent) with this language, sometimes 0BSD is included and sometimes not. \r\n\r\n@VanL - are you still involved with Python Foundation? Does \"dual licensed under the PSF License Agreement and the Zero-Clause BSD license.\" mean the examples, recipes, and other code in documentation are licensed under *both*(and) licenses or a *choice* (or)?\r\n\r\nIf the latter, then we would add as two different licenses (one with 0BSD and one without 0BSD).\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/867787139/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/943529171","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200#issuecomment-943529171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200","id":943529171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE844PRzT","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-10-14T16:39:04Z","updated_at":"2021-10-14T16:39:04Z","body":"@VanL - can you answer the above question or maybe let us know who might be able to?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/943529171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1029333500","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200#issuecomment-1029333500","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200","id":1029333500,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE849WmH8","user":{"login":"brettcannon","id":54418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon","html_url":"https://github.com/brettcannon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2022-02-03T19:37:24Z","updated_at":"2022-02-03T19:37:24Z","body":"I reached out to @VanL and he said:\r\n\r\n> Generally that sort of dual license is considered disjunctive. A person can decide to \"take\" under one of the licenses or the other. It also doesn't have to be consistent. You can take under BSD for one project and under PSF for another.\r\n For licenses that are as similar as the PSF and BSD (in terms of requirements, not text) you can just include the text of both licenses and defer the decision and effectively take under both.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1029333500/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1050048012","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200#issuecomment-1050048012","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200","id":1050048012,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE84-lnYM","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-24T16:43:42Z","updated_at":"2022-02-24T16:43:42Z","body":"A bit more research on this, and possibly duplicating what folks have already found. Using Google cache URLs in a few places below as the original URLs are throwing 503 errors at the moment.\r\n\r\nRegarding the Python \"license stack's\" use of [`CNRI-Python`](https://spdx.org/licenses/CNRI-Python.html) (shorter section 7) vs. [`CNRI-Python-GPL-Compatible`](https://spdx.org/licenses/CNRI-Python-GPL-Compatible.html) (longer section 7):\r\n\r\n* It looks like Python release 1.6 first added CNRI-Python to the mix: see [FAQ](https://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:hE4lNdHMHDwJ:https://www.python.org/download/releases/1.6/license-faq/) and [release page](https://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:2S3jm-0BMTcJ:https://www.python.org/download/releases/1.6/), with [original license text](http://www.handle.net/python_licenses/python1.6_9-5-00.html) from the \"view license\" link on the release page.\r\n* For Python release 1.6.1, it looks like they replaced CNRI-Python with CNRI-Python-GPL-Compatible: see [release page](https://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:oGgvhDcQz50J:https://www.python.org/download/releases/1.6.1/) and [original license text for 1.6.1](http://www.handle.net/python_licenses/python1.6.1-2-23-01.html).\r\n\r\nSo if that's correct, the text on the license list for [Python-2.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/Python-2.0.html) -- I'm guessing originating from the [OSI page for Python-2.0](https://opensource.org/licenses/Python-2.0) -- was actually never used for Python release 2.0. Sigh.\r\n\r\nI don't think we can replace the text of Python-2.0, or add this changed version of the CNRI portion as \"optional\" text for Python-2.0, since it certainly appears to have a different substantive legal effect if it's present vs. absent.\r\n\r\nI think all that points in the direction of:\r\n* adding one (or more) new Python-* and/or PSF-* license IDs\r\n* adding clarifying text to the Notes sections of those new IDs and also Python-2.0\r\n* (perhaps?) deprecating Python-2.0 as an identifier -- leaving it on the list as a valid identifier, but moving it down to the \"deprecated\" section so that it's less prominent?\r\n\r\n\"More discussion is warranted\" I fear...","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1050048012/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1050147025","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200#issuecomment-1050147025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200","id":1050147025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE84-l_jR","user":{"login":"brettcannon","id":54418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon","html_url":"https://github.com/brettcannon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brettcannon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2022-02-24T18:37:39Z","updated_at":"2022-02-24T18:37:39Z","body":"> * It looks like Python release 1.6 first added CNRI-Python to the mix\r\n\r\nCorrect. The Python 1.6.0 release was actually specifically for the license update.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> * For Python release 1.6.1, it looks like they replaced CNRI-Python with CNRI-Python-GPL-Compatible\r\n\r\nQuite possible. There was disagreement with GNU about GPL compatibility at one point.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> * adding one (or more) new Python-* and/or PSF-* license IDs\r\n\r\nIf you need to choose a prefix, I would suggest \"PSF\" since that's what the license is known by in the Python community and as official of a name as it has: https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/4dc746310bd37ad6b381f9176acd167d445f4385/LICENSE#L62-L63 .","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1050147025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1203325812","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200#issuecomment-1203325812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200","id":1203325812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85HuUt0","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-02T23:46:23Z","updated_at":"2022-08-02T23:46:23Z","body":"Hi all - thanks to everyone above for all the research and sorry this got procrastinated, I've cleared the \"waiting for steward\" label which wasn't helping!\r\n\r\nI've created a PR to add the Python-2.0.1 license with some markup that should then match to the various examples cited above. See #1549 for more info\r\n\r\nAlso added an updated note for Python-2.0","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1203325812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1212070718","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200#issuecomment-1212070718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1200","id":1212070718,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85IPrs-","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-11T14:31:48Z","updated_at":"2022-08-11T14:31:48Z","body":"With #1549 merged to add `Python-2.0.1` as of the 3.18 release (upcoming shortly), I believe we can close this. If there are additional edits or changes needed for `Python-2.0.1` or additional licenses to handle other cases, please open a separate issue. Thanks all!","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1212070718/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]